  {
   "text": "How do you remove a plugin from a running program, without restarting it?",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "In V.S. Code, eighty-seven of the top one hundred extensions run code, and removing one means restarting the whole extension host.",
   "seed": 8,
   "ratio": 0.878,
   "diff": [
    "replace: 'eightyseven' \u2192 '87'",
    "replace: 'one hundred' \u2192 '100'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Every cache and connection is lost.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "A new paper splits the problem in two.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "First, time: when a component leaves, everything it changed must be undone.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Then space: components depend on each other, and those dependencies come and go while the program runs.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "For time, the answer is a revertible effect.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Every change a component makes, like adding a command or opening a connection, hands the runtime its inverse.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 0.944,
   "diff": [
    "replace: 'its' \u2192 \"it's\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The runtime keeps them in a stack.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "To remove the component, it runs the stack backwards, and the program is back exactly as it was.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "For space, the answer is a reactive coeffect.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 0.824,
   "diff": [
    "replace: 'coeffect' \u2192 'co effect'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A component declares what it needs, say, a database.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "It waits, inactive, until a provider shows up, then it activates.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "If the database goes away, the component deactivates, and its effects are undone too.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Both ideas run through one shared context.",
   "seed": 8,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Every effect and every dependency passes through it, so components can come and go without disturbing each other.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
   "diff": []
  },
  {
   "text": "The authors built this as Cordis.",
   "seed": 7,
   "ratio": 1.0,
